    "raw_public_english_response": "The plan was submitted and the arm returned a normalization receipt (case sha `fcd16d76...`, proposal sha `3ddd66ad...`). The normalizer canonicalized `settings.freq` from `null` to `false`; all source literals (`B3LYP`, `aug-mcc-pV8Z`) were preserved.\n\n**Outcome — `blocked_unverified_setting`**\n\nEvidence gathered in this read-only arm:\n- **`method.functional = B3LYP`** → `exact_registered` (loader accepted, renderer preserved); evidence ceiling `loader_renderer_verification_only` (`engine_executed: false`, `scientific_adequacy_verified: false`, `setting_combination_verified: false`).\n- **`method.basis = aug-mcc-pV8Z`** → `exact_registered`, capability `orca.basis.bse.augmccpv8z` — a BSE-discovered name — with the same loader/renderer-only evidence ceiling.\n- Inventory view confirms `aug-mcc-pV8Z` is present among the six aug-mcc basis values, i.e. discoverable but not natively materialized.\n\nRationale: the `exact_registered` receipt discharges only its declared loader/renderer rule (`scientific_settings.exact_registered`); it cannot discharge any materialization/native-readiness rule. BSE name discovery was therefore **not** treated as native/compiler readiness, and no engine-execution, scientific-adequacy, or combination evidence exists in this arm to close the materialization gap for `aug-mcc-pV8Z` in ORCA. Consequently:\n\n- No project candidate, no native input, no command, no project write, no execution requested (all flags `false`).\n- `element_findings` empty (no element literals in scope); no other settings were in scope.\n- Blocking rule ids left empty — the arm exposed no concrete materialization rule id, and none was invented.",
